-- title:
--   Base change of the X₀(Mp) chart algebra to ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ with $p\nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of $L\subset L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $\varpi$ a generator of the maximal ideal, and suppose $K_2$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower; let $j_2\in K_2$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). The assertion is the existence of: a ring homomorphism $e:L\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose elements are exactly the range of $e$; a valuation subring $A^\flat$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, containing $e(A)$, with $e(a)$ in the maximal ideal of $A^\flat$ if and only if $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, and with $A^\flat\cap K$ (the ring [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.coeffSubring`](def/ModularCurve_NodeDescent.html#L10)) equal to $e(A)$; an element $\varpi^\flat=e(\varpi)$ of that ring whose multiples are exactly the elements killed by the residue map of $A^\flat$ restricted to it; a unit $\varepsilon$ with $p=(\varpi^\flat)^{p-1}\varepsilon$ there; the identification of [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.fieldOver (M * p) K`](def/ModularCurve_NodeDescent.html#L18) — the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the constant series from $K$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $Mp$ — with the image of $K_2$ under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffMap e`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16); an algebra structure of $A^\flat\cap K$ on that field whose structure map is the constant-series embedding; a nonzero element $j_K$ of it with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15); and a ring isomorphism $\Phi$ from `chartAlgFin A ↥K₂ j₂`, the subalgebra of elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$, onto `chartAlgFin` of $A^\flat\cap K$ in `fieldOver (M * p) K` at $j_K$, compatible with $q$-expansions along `coeffMap e`; and, finally, a ring isomorphism $\Psi$ from the same chart algebra onto [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.jIntegralClosure (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_NodeDescent.html#L26) $A^\flat$ $K$, the elements of `fieldOver (M * p) K` integral over [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.jRing`](def/ModularCurve_NodeDescent.html#L22) $A^\flat$ $K$, again compatible with $q$-expansions.
--
--   This transports the finite chart algebra of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(Mp)$ over the cyclotomic discrete valuation ring $A$ to a valuation-theoretic setting inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, producing simultaneously the coefficient data $(\varpi^\flat,\ p-1,\ \varepsilon)$, the level field $K(j,j_{Mp})$ and the corresponding $j$-integral closure. It feeds the computation of the completed local ring at a node of $X_0(Mp)$ above a supersingular point, where the crossing model and the width–thickness relation are read off.
